prism, height coordinate of the prism,
base
In this paper, the term “prism” refers to the n-dimensional region formed when an (n–1)-dimensional polyhedron (the base) is dragged
along a line segment extending into the remaining dimension. The
direction of the dragging is the “height coordinate” of the prism.
