semidirect product
Let G be a group with subgroup F and normal subgroup N. G is the
semidirect product N F iff every element in G can be written in one
and only one way as the product fn, with f F and n N. See a group theory textbook for details.
involution A function F is an involution iff F(F(a)) = a.
isometry A function F is an isometry iff the distance between F(a) and F(b) is
