For any maximally even chord {m0, m1, ..., mn-1}, and any integer d, the set {mi + d (mod n) – mi} will contain either a single integer-valued point in
R/kZ or a pair of adjacent integer-valued points in R/kZ. The n-note
maximally even subsets of a chromatic scale are related by transposition.
